// THE SEARCH PATH, AND WHAT '--path' ADDS TO IT. A name no file beside the
// importer answers is looked for on the package search path: each '--path' folder
// in order, then the packages folder, where core and stdio are. This scenario's
// run passes '--path=test/cases/module/modulepkgs', whose stdio is not the
// packages folder's, and it is the one 'import stdio' reaches: 'show' is a
// function only it declares.
//
// '--path' adds to the search path and replaces nothing, so core is still found
// in the packages folder, as it must be for any program to compile.
//
// It RUNS: a module found on the search path is compiled into this object, so the
// package's function is defined here and the call links.

mod module_package_path;

import stdio;

fn main() i32 {
  stdio.show("path-stdio", 7i64);
  0i32;
}
